#op: load
#dir: operations/get/query
#history-at: .history/operations/get/query
A tool that keeps a lineage's history apart from its tip reads it with
`authoring.HistoryAt`, or `load.HistoryAt` for the one-call loaders: the
versions are read from the history/ under that directory, in place of the
lineage's own. A lineage has one history, so .thema files in its own
directory's history/ as well are refused rather than ignored. Here 0.0 is
in both.
-- operations/get/query/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
}
-- operations/get/query/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
}
-- .history/operations/get/query/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
}
